[DOCUMENT]
TITLE: Functional Requirements
PREFIX: FR-

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-001
STATEMENT: >>>
Process VT/xterm escape sequences using the Ghostty parser (`libghostty-vt`).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-002
STATEMENT: >>>
Maintain a terminal grid data model (`Grid`) consisting of rows of cells, each with a character code, foreground/background color, and text attributes (`Attrs`).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-003
STATEMENT: >>>
Support SGR (Select Graphic Rendition) parameters: bold, dim, italic, underline, double underline, blink, reverse, hidden, strikethrough, overline, and protected.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-004
STATEMENT: >>>
Support 16 ANSI color palette indices plus 256-color and truecolor (24-bit RGB) foreground/background specifications.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-005
STATEMENT: >>>
Support alternate screen buffer mode (SM/RM 1049) for full-screen applications (e.g., vim, less).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-006
STATEMENT: >>>
Support cursor positioning and movement (CUU, CUD, CUF, CUB, CUP, HVP, etc.) and cursor style (block, bar, underline, beam) with visible/hidden state.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-007
STATEMENT: >>>
Support scrolling regions (`scroll_up`, `scroll_down`, `insert_lines`, `delete_lines`) with configurable top/bottom boundaries.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-008
STATEMENT: >>>
Support tab stops (set, clear, move).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-009
STATEMENT: >>>
Report terminal size changes via `SIGWINCH` to the child process.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-010
STATEMENT: >>>
Render the terminal grid using wgpu (Vulkan) as the sole graphics backend. OpenGL and CPU software paths are not supported.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-011
STATEMENT: >>>
Shape text runs using `cosmic-text` and rasterize glyphs using `swash`, caching results in a GPU atlas.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-012
STATEMENT: >>>
Pack glyph bitmaps into a GPU texture atlas using `guillotiere` for dynamic rectangle allocation and eviction.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-013
STATEMENT: >>>
Maintain a dirty mask (`DirtyMask`) that tracks which rows of the grid have changed and limit rendering to those rows.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-014
STATEMENT: >>>
Render a cell cursor (block, bar, underline, beam) with configurable color and blink behavior.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-015
STATEMENT: >>>
Render text selection highlights (character, word, line, block modes) as colored overlays on the affected cells.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-016
STATEMENT: >>>
Support font configuration: family, size, line spacing, and fallback to preferred monospace fonts (Roboto Mono, JetBrains Mono, etc.).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-017
STATEMENT: >>>
Render the terminal background, foreground, and 16-color ANSI palette from the active theme configuration.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-018
STATEMENT: >>>
Recover from GPU surface destruction (e.g., Android activity restart) by recreating the render pipeline and continuing without data loss.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-019
STATEMENT: >>>
Support the Kitty Graphics Protocol (KGP) for rendering inline images as textured quads.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-020
STATEMENT: >>>
Encode physical keyboard input using the Kitty Keyboard Protocol (KBP) for extended modifier and key reporting.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-021
STATEMENT: >>>
Support IME (Input Method Editor) text input for composing CJK and other complex characters, with `Composing` state management.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-022
STATEMENT: >>>
Support terminal selection in four modes: character (`Char`), word (`Word`), line (`Line`), and block (`Block`).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-023
STATEMENT: >>>
Automatically expand word-mode selections to word boundaries and detect URLs (`http://`, `https://`, `ftp://`, `www.`) for URL-aware selection expansion.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-024
STATEMENT: >>>
Support touch input gestures: tap to place cursor, long-press for selection handles, and swipe for scrollback navigation.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-025
STATEMENT: >>>
Send DEL (`0x7F`) for the backspace key and encode modifier keys (Ctrl/Shift/Alt/Super) per the Kitty keyboard protocol.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-026
STATEMENT: >>>
Spawn a child process (shell or custom executable) connected to a pseudo-terminal (PTY) via `fork/exec`.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-027
STATEMENT: >>>
Read PTY output on a dedicated reader thread and forward parsed output to the grid update pipeline via a `flume` channel.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-028
STATEMENT: >>>
Wait for child process exit on a dedicated waiter thread and emit a `ProcessExited` event on termination.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-029
STATEMENT: >>>
Support resizing a terminal session (changing rows and columns) and forwarding the new size to the child process via `SIGWINCH`.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-030
STATEMENT: >>>
Maintain a bounded scrollback buffer with a configurable maximum (default 50,000 lines), evicting oldest entries when the limit is exceeded.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-031
STATEMENT: >>>
Support a scrollback search feature that finds text matching a pattern (regex or literal) within the scrollback history.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-032
STATEMENT: >>>
Clear the scrollback buffer when entering the alternate screen and restore it on exit.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-033
STATEMENT: >>>
Intercept OSC 7 sequences (`ESC ] 7 ; <uri> ST`) and extract the current working directory path as a `CwdEvent`.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-034
STATEMENT: >>>
Intercept OSC 8 sequences (`ESC ] 8 ; <params> ; <url> ST`) and extract hyperlink open/close events as `HyperlinkEvent`.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-035
STATEMENT: >>>
Intercept OSC 52 sequences (`ESC ] 52 ; <selection> ; <base64> ST`) and decode clipboard content as a `ClipboardEvent`.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-036
STATEMENT: >>>
Intercept OSC 9 (iTerm2) and OSC 777 (rxvt) sequences and extract notification title/body as `NotificationEvent`.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-037
STATEMENT: >>>
Pass through unrecognised OSC sequences (e.g., OSC 0 for title, OSC 4 for palette change) to the VT parser unchanged.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-038
STATEMENT: >>>
Handle partial OSC sequences that arrive split across multiple input chunks, accumulating state across `process()` calls.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-039
STATEMENT: >>>
Copy selected text to the system clipboard on user request (e.g., copy action from selection).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-040
STATEMENT: >>>
Read clipboard content when requested by terminal applications via OSC 52 (paste).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-041
STATEMENT: >>>
Display Android notifications for terminal-emitted OSC 9/777 notification sequences.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-042
STATEMENT: >>>
Provide an executable (`exec-bin`) capable of establishing SSH and Mosh connections.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-043
STATEMENT: >>>
Integrate SSH/Mosh sessions with the terminal session lifecycle (PTY management, resize forwarding).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-044
STATEMENT: >>>
Run an MCP (Model Context Protocol) server over a Unix domain socket, communicating via JSON-RPC 2.0 with newline-delimited JSON.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-045
STATEMENT: >>>
Expose tools for listing sessions, reading grid state, reading scrollback, reading cursor position, and reading selected text.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-046
STATEMENT: >>>
Expose tools for writing to the PTY, sending signals, resizing the terminal, and setting clipboard content (gated behind `--mcp-allow-write`).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-047
STATEMENT: >>>
Expose a scrollback search tool that matches a regex pattern and returns matching line numbers, text, and column ranges.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-048
STATEMENT: >>>
Expose an input queue mechanism that watches for a prompt pattern in scrollback and automatically injects queued text (AI agent automation).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-049
STATEMENT: >>>
Use JNI for NDK-level functions (ANativeWindow lifecycle, surface creation/destruction) via `ffi.rs`.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-050
STATEMENT: >>>
Handle Android surface creation and destruction events, recreating the wgpu surface and render pipeline as needed.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-051
STATEMENT: >>>
Support ProGuard/R8 obfuscation with `-dontoptimize` to preserve direct JNI (no JNA).
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-052
STATEMENT: >>>
Provide 16 built-in color themes: Catppuccin Mocha, Catppuccin Latte, Dracula+, Nord, Tokyo Night, Rose Pine, Gruvbox Dark, Gruvbox Light, Everforest Dark, One Dark, One Light, Monokai, Ayu Dark, Ayu Light, Kanagawa Wave, and Night Owl.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-053
STATEMENT: >>>
Support user-defined custom themes persisted in DataStore with fields for name, background, foreground, cursor, selection background, and 16 ANSI color slots.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-054
STATEMENT: >>>
Support configuration of terminal dimensions (rows, cols), scrollback size, shell path, and font size via `TerminalConfig`.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-055
STATEMENT: >>>
Repository SHALL NOT contain golden images; rendering verification SHALL use logical assertions or OCR.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-056
STATEMENT: >>>
The crate SHALL provide an off-screen render-verification path — a procedural geometry generator (`SceneData` + floor/sphere/box/torus + hand-written matrix helpers) and an infinite LOD grid shader rendered through a `Depth32Float` attachment — used by crate tests to verify GPU rendering and depth attachment behavior. This path SHALL NOT add depth attachments to the production terminal render path.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-057
STATEMENT: >>>
The search overlay input SHALL debounce query changes by 150 ms (Handler-based) so the native scrollback search only runs after the user pauses typing.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-058
STATEMENT: >>>
Dependent settings controls SHALL be grayed out (disabled) when their prerequisite is off — the cursor-speed slider when cursor blink is off, and the user-theme edit entry when no user themes exist.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-059
STATEMENT: >>>
The terminal surface SHALL expose accessibility custom actions (read previous line, read next line, read all) and update its content description to the current screen text (throttled) so TalkBack can navigate terminal content line by line.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-060
STATEMENT: >>>
The bootstrap installer SHALL support both HTTP download and local-file install (SAF), and SHALL offer an offline path reading the bootstrap archive from `assets/bootstrap/` when present (no network). Embedded assets SHALL be detected at runtime; the APK SHALL NOT be forced to carry the archive.
<<<

[REQUIREMENT]
UID: FR-061
STATEMENT: >>>
Toolbar keys SHALL support a width (flex weight) and an optional secondary key (long-press action); the layout editor SHALL allow editing both; serialization SHALL be backward compatible with existing layouts.
<<<

